diff --git a/os/android/README.md b/os/android/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4e7aff4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/os/android/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@
+## OpenTTD for Android
+
+This is the regular desktop OpenTTD, packaged as an Android app. The full
+desktop interface is kept; input is designed around a mouse:
+
+- A physical mouse (USB / Bluetooth) and keyboard work as on desktop,
+  including right-drag scrolling, the scroll wheel and all hotkeys.
+- Without a mouse the touch screen acts as a **trackpad** that moves the cursor:
+
+| Gesture                              | Action                                 |
+|--------------------------------------|----------------------------------------|
+| One finger drag                      | Move the cursor                        |
+| Tap                                  | Left click                             |
+| Double tap                           | Double click                           |
+| Tap, then touch again and drag       | Drag with the left button held (e.g. build a line of track) |
+| Two finger tap                       | Right click                            |
+| Two finger drag                      | Scroll the map, or the list under the cursor |
+| Pinch                                | Zoom the map at the cursor             |
+| Three finger tap                     | Show / hide the on-screen keyboard     |
+| Back button / gesture                | Escape (close the top window)          |
+
+Savegames, scenarios, the configuration and downloaded content are stored in
+`Android/data/org.openttd.android/files/openttd/` on the device storage, which
+is accessible over USB, so files can be copied in and out. On first start the
+app offers to use an `OpenTTD` folder in the root of the device storage instead,
+which file managers can reach and which survives uninstalling. Any other folder
+can be chosen later with the "Storage location" shortcut: long-press the app icon. That needs the "All files access" permission, as OpenTTD uses
+plain file I/O; existing files can be copied to the new folder.
+The free base sets OpenGFX, OpenSFX and OpenMSX are included.
+
+### Building
+
+Requirements:
+- JDK 17 or newer,
+- the Android SDK with NDK `29.0.14206865` (see `ndkVersion` in `app/build.gradle.kts`),
+- CMake 3.31+ and Ninja on the build host, plus a host C++ compiler (for the host tools),
+- a [vcpkg](https://github.com/microsoft/vcpkg) checkout; the dependencies
+  listed in the top-level `vcpkg.json` are built for Android automatically.
+
+Create `os/android/local.properties`:
+```
+sdk.dir=/path/to/Android/Sdk
+cmake.dir=/usr
+vcpkg.root=/path/to/vcpkg
+```
+
+Then, from `os/android`:
+```
+./gradlew assembleDebug
+```
+
+The APK ends up in `app/build/outputs/apk/debug/`. Install it with
+`adb install -r app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk`.
+
+By default only `arm64-v8a` is built. To build other ABIs (e.g. `x86_64` for
+the emulator), set `openttd.abis=arm64-v8a,x86_64` in `local.properties`.
+
+The first build takes a while, as vcpkg builds all dependencies (ICU, curl,
+OpenSSL, FreeType, HarfBuzz, SDL2, ...) for each ABI; later builds use the
+vcpkg binary cache.
+
+Release builds (`./gradlew assembleRelease`) are signed with the key given by
+`openttd.keystore`, `openttd.keystorePassword`, `openttd.keyAlias` and
+`openttd.keyPassword` (Gradle properties or `local.properties`), or the
+`OPENTTD_KEYSTORE*` / `OPENTTD_KEY_*` environment variables; without one they
+are signed with the debug key. The version code is the number of commits.
+
+### Releases
+
+There are two branches:
+- `stable`: the Android port on top of the latest OpenTTD release (e.g. 15.3).
+  Releases are made from here; they identify as that OpenTTD release, so they
+  can join its multiplayer servers.
+- `main`: the Android port on top of OpenTTD's master (the development
+  version). It is built every night as the "nightly" pre-release, which
+  installs as a separate "OpenTTD Touch Nightly" app (set `openttd.nightly=true`
+  for such a build locally).
+
+`.github/workflows/deploy.yml` builds the APKs on GitHub Actions. Pushing a tag
+starting with `v` on the `stable` branch publishes it as a GitHub release:
+```
+git tag v15.3.0
+git push origin v15.3.0
+```
+The release key is taken from the repository secrets `ANDROID_KEYSTORE_BASE64`
+(the keystore, base64 encoded), `ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD`, `ANDROID_KEY_ALIAS`
+and `ANDROID_KEY_PASSWORD`. Keep the keystore safe: updates only install over
+an APK signed with the same key.
+
+### Debugging
+
+The game logs to logcat under the `OpenTTD` tag. Command line arguments can be
+passed through an intent extra, e.g. for more driver output:
+```
+adb shell am start -n org.openttd.android/.LauncherActivity --es args "'-d driver=3'"
+```
+
+### Rendering
+
+The `sdl-opengl` video driver is used, running on OpenGL ES 3.0 or newer
+(see `src/video/opengl.cpp`); when that is unavailable the game falls back to
+the software `sdl` driver.
+
+### How it fits together
+
+- `app/src/main/java/org/libsdl/app` is SDL's Java glue, taken unmodified
+  from the SDL release matching the vcpkg SDL2 port.
+- `LauncherActivity` extracts the game data (packaged as APK assets) to
+  internal storage once per installed version, then starts `OpenTTDActivity`,
+  which runs the game from `libmain.so`.
+- `src/os/android/android_main.cpp` is the native entry point: it redirects
+  stdout/stderr to logcat (`adb logcat -s OpenTTD`), sets up the directories and
+  calls the normal OpenTTD main.
+- `src/video/sdl2_touch.cpp` implements the trackpad emulation.
diff --git a/os/android/app/build.gradle.kts b/os/android/app/build.gradle.kts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f6628ba
--- /dev/null
+++ b/os/android/app/build.gradle.kts
@@ -0,0 +1,200 @@
+import java.io.FileInputStream
+import java.net.URI
+import java.util.Properties
+import java.util.zip.ZipInputStream
+
+plugins {
+    id("com.android.application")
+}
+
+/* The OpenTTD source tree; this project lives in os/android. */
+val openttdRoot: File = rootDir.resolve("../..").canonicalFile
+
+val localProperties = Properties().apply {
+    val file = rootDir.resolve("local.properties")
+    if (file.exists()) FileInputStream(file).use { load(it) }
+}
+
+/** Look up a setting as Gradle property, in local.properties, or as environment variable. */
+fun setting(name: String, env: String): String? =
+    (findProperty(name) as String?) ?: localProperties.getProperty(name) ?: System.getenv(env)
+
+val vcpkgRoot = setting("vcpkg.root", "VCPKG_ROOT")
+    ?: throw GradleException("Point vcpkg.root (local.properties) or VCPKG_ROOT to a vcpkg checkout; see README.md")
+
+/* Comma separated list of ABIs to build; arm64-v8a covers practically all current devices. */
+val abis = (setting("openttd.abis", "OPENTTD_ABIS") ?: "arm64-v8a").split(",").map { it.trim() }
+
+/* Version from the project() call in the main CMakeLists.txt: an indented line like "    VERSION 16.0". */
+val openttdVersion: String = Regex("""(?m)^\s+VERSION\s+(\d+)\.(\d+)""")
+    .find(openttdRoot.resolve("CMakeLists.txt").readText())!!.let { "${it.groupValues[1]}.${it.groupValues[2]}" }
+
+/* Always increasing version code for Android: the number of commits. */
+val commitCount: Int = runCatching {
+    providers.exec { commandLine("git", "-C", openttdRoot.path, "rev-list", "--count", "HEAD") }
+        .standardOutput.asText.get().trim().toInt()
+}.getOrDefault(1)
+
+/* Nightly builds are a separate app, so they can be installed next to the stable release. */
+val nightly = setting("openttd.nightly", "OPENTTD_NIGHTLY").let { it == "1" || it == "true" }
+
+/* Release signing key, e.g. from CI secrets; without it release builds are signed with the debug key. */
+val releaseKeystore = setting("openttd.keystore", "OPENTTD_KEYSTORE")
+
+val hostToolsDir: File = layout.buildDirectory.dir("host-tools").get().asFile
+val gameDataDir: File = layout.buildDirectory.dir("generated/game-data").get().asFile
+val vcpkgInstalledDir: File = layout.buildDirectory.dir("vcpkg_installed").get().asFile
+
+android {
+    namespace = "org.openttd.android"
+    compileSdk = 36
+    ndkVersion = "29.0.14206865"
+
+    defaultConfig {
+        applicationId = "org.openttd.android"
+        minSdk = 28
+        targetSdk = 36
+        versionCode = commitCount
+        versionName = setting("openttd.versionName", "OPENTTD_VERSION_NAME") ?: "$openttdVersion-android"
+        if (nightly) applicationIdSuffix = ".nightly"
+        resValue("string", "app_name", if (nightly) "OpenTTD Touch Nightly" else "OpenTTD Touch")
+
+        ndk {
+            abiFilters += abis
+        }
+
+        externalNativeBuild {
+            cmake {
+                arguments += listOf(
+                    "-DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=${rootDir.resolve("cmake/android-vcpkg-toolchain.cmake")}",
+                    "-DVCPKG_ROOT=$vcpkgRoot",
+                    "-DVCPKG_INSTALLED_DIR=$vcpkgInstalledDir",
+                    "-DHOST_BINARY_DIR=$hostToolsDir",
+                    "-DANDROID_ASSETS_DIR=$gameDataDir",
+                    "-DANDROID_STL=c++_shared",
+                    "-DOPTION_USE_ASSERTS=OFF",
+                )
+                targets += "openttd"
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    signingConfigs {
+        if (releaseKeystore != null) {
+            create("release") {
+                storeFile = file(releaseKeystore)
+                storePassword = setting("openttd.keystorePassword", "OPENTTD_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD")
+                keyAlias = setting("openttd.keyAlias", "OPENTTD_KEY_ALIAS")
+                keyPassword = setting("openttd.keyPassword", "OPENTTD_KEY_PASSWORD")
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    buildTypes {
+        debug {
+            externalNativeBuild {
+                cmake {
+                    /* An unoptimised OpenTTD is unplayable; keep debug info but optimise. */
+                    arguments += "-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo"
+                }
+            }
+        }
+        release {
+            isMinifyEnabled = false
+            /* Without a release key, sign with the debug key so the build can still be sideloaded. */
+            signingConfig = signingConfigs.findByName("release") ?: signingConfigs.getByName("debug")
+            externalNativeBuild {
+                cmake {
+                    arguments += "-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release"
+                }
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    externalNativeBuild {
+        cmake {
+            path = openttdRoot.resolve("CMakeLists.txt")
+        }
+    }
+
+    sourceSets {
+        getByName("main") {
+            assets.srcDirs(gameDataDir)
+        }
+    }
+
+    buildFeatures {
+        resValues = true
+    }
+
+    compileOptions {
+        sourceCompatibility = JavaVersion.VERSION_17
+        targetCompatibility = JavaVersion.VERSION_17
+    }
+
+    packaging {
+        jniLibs {
+            /* libmain.so contains the ICU data and compresses well; keep the APK small. */
+            useLegacyPackaging = true
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+/* Host tools (strgen, settingsgen) are needed to generate sources while cross-compiling. */
+val buildHostTools by tasks.registering(Exec::class) {
+    description = "Builds the OpenTTD host tools needed for cross-compiling"
+    inputs.dir(openttdRoot.resolve("src/strgen"))
+    inputs.dir(openttdRoot.resolve("src/settingsgen"))
+    outputs.dir(hostToolsDir)
+    commandLine("sh", "-c",
+        "cmake -S '$openttdRoot' -B '$hostToolsDir' -DOPTION_TOOLS_ONLY=ON -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release && " +
+        "cmake --build '$hostToolsDir' --target tools --parallel")
+}
+
+/* Free base sets, so the game is playable without the original TTD data files. */
+abstract class DownloadBaseSets : DefaultTask() {
+    @get:Input
+    abstract val baseSets: ListProperty<String>
+
+    @get:OutputDirectory
+    abstract val outputDir: DirectoryProperty
+
+    @TaskAction
+    fun download() {
+        val target = outputDir.get().asFile.resolve("openttd/baseset")
+        target.mkdirs()
+        for (path in baseSets.get()) {
+            /* Each zip contains a single .tar, which OpenTTD reads directly. */
+            URI("https://cdn.openttd.org/$path").toURL().openStream().use { stream ->
+                ZipInputStream(stream).use { zip ->
+                    generateSequence { zip.nextEntry }.filter { !it.isDirectory }.forEach { entry ->
+                        target.resolve(File(entry.name).name).outputStream().use { zip.copyTo(it) }
+                    }
+                }
+            }
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+val downloadBaseSets by tasks.registering(DownloadBaseSets::class) {
+    description = "Downloads OpenGFX, OpenSFX and OpenMSX"
+    baseSets.set(listOf(
+        "opengfx-releases/8.0/opengfx-8.0-all.zip",
+        "opensfx-releases/1.0.3/opensfx-1.0.3-all.zip",
+        "openmsx-releases/0.4.2/openmsx-0.4.2-all.zip",
+    ))
+}
+
+androidComponents {
+    onVariants { variant ->
+        variant.sources.assets?.addGeneratedSourceDirectory(downloadBaseSets, DownloadBaseSets::outputDir)
+    }
+}
+
+tasks.configureEach {
+    if (name.startsWith("configureCMake")) dependsOn(buildHostTools)
+    /* The game data is produced by the native build (see ANDROID_ASSETS_DIR in CMakeLists.txt). */
+    Regex("merge(\\w+)Assets").matchEntire(name)?.let {
+        dependsOn("externalNativeBuild${it.groupValues[1]}")
+    }
+}
